  "later_semantic_clarifications": [
    {
      "verification": "verification-84045484d691",
      "candidate_git_head": "8bd88d7b48112c1c4a652d4d278abe8e1aa0ae5d",
      "facts": "Current-candidate clarification after verification-84045484d691: 35 of 39 groups pass, with installation passed. The three non-resource failed groups have these observed causes. These facts refine public interface behavior and are statically checked by the host against the pinned original. No original implementation, test programs, or reserved cases are supplied.\n\n1. Cached speech model download bookkeeping is PER LOAD REQUEST, not once per process or once per repository for the lifetime of a process. Each call resolving the default speech weights records a best-effort config.json request with force_download=True, even when the weight archive is already cached. Two consecutive load requests therefore produce two bookkeeping requests while reusing the same local weights. The earlier wording 'once-per-repository' meant the relevant repository's event for a load, not global memoization across loads. Do not keep a persistent already-registered-repositories cache. Failures in this bookkeeping remain nonfatal. Preserve the already-fixed named repo_id and filename arguments.\n\n2. Live microphone listening has its OWN visible recording, Enter to stop prompt. It must be printed while capture is active and remain visible when input() is replaced; the separate record() function is already repaired. Live rendering also preserves the pending transcript string's whitespace exactly as supplied by the streaming result, including leading whitespace. Do not strip the provisional pending text. Preserve real streaming, committed text, keyword option forwarding, resampling, cleanup and worker-error propagation.\n\n3. The public needle.agent.whistle.languages(weights) result is an ordered TUPLE, including when a newly trained archive contains an extra language. Its fallback stays the existing LANGUAGES tuple. Parse actual archive contents and convert the discovered sequence to the required tuple; do not return a list or hardcode language extensions. Both remaining speech-training groups completed training/export and failed at this public return-type comparison; preserve the already-working actual optimization, learned vocabulary, archive, and scoring implementation.\n\nThe environment group still awaits host-supplied cases.json. Do not read or invent those payloads. Earlier download/platform and generation failures now pass; preserve those repairs. These observations do not establish that the next candidate passes. The unchanged original baseline remains valid for candidate-only repairs, and a full current-candidate comparison plus fresh installation will be required after the final data integration. No size-only optimization.",
